# Tell Git to treat these as binary so it doesn't try to do line-ending
# conversion or text diffs on them. Critical for game assets — Windows
# Git would otherwise corrupt PNGs by rewriting LF<->CRLF.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.svg binary
*.mp3 binary
*.wav binary
*.ogg binary
*.m4a binary
*.mp4 binary
*.webm binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.zip binary
*.psd binary
# 3D models. Almost all .glb are gitignored (see .gitignore), but the
# containment lab's two characters are an explicit exception and ship in the
# repo — and a GLB is a binary container whose JSON chunk length is a byte
# count. Line-ending rewriting on Windows would shift every offset after it and
# produce a file that parses as garbage rather than one that obviously fails.
*.glb binary

# HTML and JS are text — let Git normalize line endings as needed
*.html text
*.css text
*.js text
*.json text
*.md text
